<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 185,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 185,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 100,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 45,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat, 40,000 tonnes of Australian wheat and 40,000 tonnes of Canadian barley at its weekly tender, all for February shipment.</p>
<p>The tender results details are as follows, in tonnes.</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 100,000	  Western white	    40,000</p>
<p>				   Dark northern spring   40,000</p>
<p>				   Hard red winter</p>
<p>				    (11.5 percent protein)20,000</p>
<p> Canada     45,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>								  27,000</p>
<p>				   Durum			18,000</p>
<p> Australia  40,000	   Standard white	   40,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> Canada     40,000	   Feed			 30,000</p>
<p>				   Food			 10,000</p>
</text>
